From a00ef95204d07976670b5116af196292b405b7d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Review <review@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:21:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] tu: Mark compute state stale when a secondary executes
 mesh draws

compute_program_stale is only set in tu_mesh_draw() on the command buffer
that records the draw. A secondary command buffer executed inside a render
pass appends its draw CS to the primary's, so the mesh compute programs
overwrite the primary's bound compute pipeline at render pass end, but the
primary never learns about it: its next vkCmdDispatch skips re-emitting the
compute shader state and runs with the mesh/setup shader's state.

tu_render_pass_state_merge() is where the primary absorbs the secondary's
render pass state (it already merges has_mesh), so set the flag there.
tu_dispatch() already marks COMPUTE_DESC_SETS dirty when it sees the flag.

Not verified: that tu_CmdExecuteCommands() calls this merge for every
secondary executed inside a render pass on the Mesa base 4da08cb.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index f7ab5ab..f9d917e 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -6340,6 +6340,12 @@ tu6_emit_descriptor_sets(struct tu_cmd_buffer *cmd,
    dst->xfb_used |= src->xfb_used;
    dst->has_tess |= src->has_tess;
    dst->has_mesh |= src->has_mesh;
+   /* A secondary's mesh draws run compute shaders in the draw CS that is
+    * appended to ours, so our bound compute pipeline is clobbered too. The
+    * secondary's own flag is not visible to the primary's dispatches.
+    */
+   if (src->has_mesh)
+      cmd->state.compute_program_stale = true;
    dst->has_prim_generated_query_in_rp |= src->has_prim_generated_query_in_rp;
    dst->has_vtx_stats_query_in_rp |= src->has_vtx_stats_query_in_rp;
    dst->has_zpass_done_sample_count_write_in_rp |= src->has_zpass_done_sample_count_write_in_rp;
